@namespace Jewel.JPMS.Features.Triage.Panels

@*
    System actions — the place where specific actions will be lined up against an email and fired
    when its triage completes. Deliberately a shell for now: the form components it will host live
    elsewhere in the app and are being brought across in a code-reuse refactor, so this pane only
    stakes out the ground (and keeps the icon honest) rather than wiring anything to Apply.
*@

<div class="panel p-6 space-y-3">
    <div>
        <p class="eyebrow mb-1">System actions</p>
        <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-content">Line up actions for when triage completes</h2>
    </div>
    <p class="text-sm text-content-muted">
        This is where specific system actions will be staged against the open email — queued here,
        then actioned automatically when the email's triage is applied.
    </p>
    <p class="text-sm text-content-subtle">
        Nothing can be staged yet: the action forms are being brought across from their current
        homes so they can be reused here without duplication. The window itself already behaves
        like the others — load it either side, resize, and it keeps its place.
    </p>
</div>
